  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Draw**: Start your turn by taking one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. **Meld** (optional): Lay one or more valid combinations face upâ€”sets (3â€“4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive in suit). 3. **Lay off** (optional): Add cards to your own or others' melds. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by placing one card face-up on the discard pile. If you drew from the discard, you cannot discard that same card to leave the pile unchanged. 5. **Going out**: First to meld, lay off, or discard away all cards wins the hand. Play stops immediately.",
    Player: "1. **Draw**: Start your turn by taking one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. **Meld** (optional): Lay one or more valid combinations face upâ€”sets (3â€“4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive in suit). 3. **Lay off** (optional): Add cards to your own or others' melds. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by placing one card face-up on the discard pile. If you drew from the discard, you cannot discard that same card to leave the pile unchanged. 5. **Going out**: First to meld, lay off, or discard away all cards wins the hand. Play stops immediately.",
    objective: 'Dispose of all cards in your hand by melding, laying off, and discarding. Go out first; others count deadwood (unmelded cards) as penalty points.',
    gameplay: "1. **Draw**: Start your turn by taking one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. **Meld** (optional): Lay one or more valid combinations face upâ€”sets (3â€“4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive in suit). 3. **Lay off** (optional): Add cards to your own or others' melds. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by placing one card face-up on the discard pile. If you drew from the discard, you cannot discard that same card to leave the pile unchanged. 5. **Going out**: First to meld, lay off, or discard away all cards wins the hand. Play stops immediately.",
    keyRules: [
      'Melds: Sets = 3â€“4 of same rank. Runs = 3+ consecutive same suit (A-2-3 valid; Q-K-A usually not unless house rule).',
      'One meld per turn (unless house rule allows multiple).',
      'Lay off is optional; can add to any meld on the table.',
      'Cannot discard the same card you just took from the discard pile if that would leave the pile unchanged.',
      "When stock runs out and next player doesn't want the discard, discard pile is turned over (unshuffled) as new stock.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
