    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Dispose of all cards in your hand by melding, laying off, and discarding. Go out first; others count deadwood (unmelded cards) as penalty points.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Draw**: Start your turn by taking one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. **Meld** (optional): Lay one or more valid combinations face upâ€”sets (3â€“4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive in suit). 3. **Lay off** (optional): Add cards to your own or others' melds. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by placing one card face-up on the discard pile. If you drew from the discard, you cannot discard that same card to leave the pile unchanged. 5. **Going out**: First to meld, lay off, or discard away all cards wins the hand. Play stops immediately.",
      "Scoring example: When a player goes out, others sum the point value of cards left in hand. Number cards = face value. Aces = 1. Face cards (J,Q,K) = 10. Total is added to the winner's score. Game continues until target score or agreed deals. First to reach the agreed target score wins the game. Each hand: winner scores the sum of opponents' deadwood..",
